  "surprise": "746 at 8 loops (746/766/725) against 510's 764 (743/815/734): -18, discard. Seeds 0 and 2 moved +3 and -9; the mean loss is seed 1 (-49 against the loop's high outlier 815). The pre-registered 'parameters are the bottleneck' reading is falsified: the mean is below 764 and per-sample dev accuracy at 8 loops is within 0.01 of 510's on two seeds (0.467/0.442/0.444 against 0.461/0.481/0.443; seed 1 -0.039), so matching the untied control's parameter count (9,580,544 against 590's 9,558,528) with a wider tied trunk does not close the gap to 792. With 506 (untied first pass, 9.56M, -25) this is the second way of spending the spare 3.2M that bought nothing, and this one changed neither the architecture nor the loop schedule nor the RL. Pretraining went the capacity way, RL did not. Val loss at 2 loops 0.0791/0.0872/0.0887 (mean 0.0850) against 0.0824/0.0894/0.0912 (0.0877), lower on every seed by 0.002-0.003 with 21% fewer steps (2,687/2,688/2,697 against 3,409/3,470/3,422; the bench said 0.79x), depth-flat within 0.0004 from 2 to 8 loops as always; held-out greedy after pretraining 0.947/0.954/0.948 (510: 0.943/0.960/0.965). The pretrained model also started RL stronger on two seeds: round-1 one-loop acceptance 0.161/0.199/0.039 (510: 0.048/0.111/0.061) and 700/731/257 targets solved after round 1 (510: 261/723/343). From round 5 on the advantage was gone: one-loop acceptance at matched rounds 5-10 was 0.569-0.647 on seed 0 against 510's 0.587-0.653 (equal or 0.01-0.02 lower), 0.575-0.646 on seed 1 against 0.579-0.664 (0.00-0.04 lower), 0.553-0.666 on seed 2 against 0.569-0.651 (mixed); last round 0.649/0.646/0.666 (510: 0.671/0.667/0.634; predicted 0.66-0.76, two seeds under). RL discovery at matched round 10 (call 40) was 1,243/1,254/1,247 against 510's 1,239/1,294/1,230 and 590's 1,264: equal within seed noise. So 1.5x the parameters in every block fit the found proofs no better per round and generalize no better per sample; the extra capacity shows only in the pretraining loss and in round 1, which (507, 509) predict nothing. Compare the control: 590's untied model reaches one-loop acceptance 0.769 at round 5 and 0.835 at round 13 under 507's recipe, where 509 (the looped trunk under the closest recipe) had 0.638 at round 5 and 0.734 at its last round, 11: the untied blocks fit their own proofs far better per round than any tied core so far, wide or narrow. That points the 792 gap at tying (the shared core's converged iteration, 505) or at RL budget (590 ran 20 rounds because its retries cost 6 blocks per token at every level), not at parameter count or pretraining fit (505 and 508 already showed lower val loss reaching nothing). Costs as predicted or milder: rounds 11/10/10 (predicted 9-11; 510: 13/14/12); rounds 3+ took 134-158/137-174/129-177 s (predicted 140-175; 510: 102-142); fine-tune 35-52 s per round at 0.128 s/step (510: 27-42 s, 0.103 s/step; predicted 55-75, too high), ft_steps 293-393 as 510; sampling slowed less than the 0.75x assumed: 1-loop 173-223 samples/s (510: 201-249), 8-loop retries 68-96 (510: 70-117), 8-loop eval 68/74/81 (510: 83/87/90); eval sampling 1,041/953/877 s at 8 loops and 541/424/406 s at 2 (510: 850/816/789 and 379/381/371); totals 4,286/4,021/3,982 s (predicted 4,300-4,700), 1,100 s inside TOTAL_SECS; no OOM at the 8-loop eval. Cumulative RL solved 1,253/1,254/1,247 (510: 1,264/1,314/1,243). Loops unchanged, as pre-registered: metric minus diag +19 (14/21/21; 510: +12 = 12/20/5), per-sample 8-vs-2 gap 0.039/0.041/0.036 (510: 0.039/0.037/0.026), retry crack rates pooled 16.3/22.0/21.2, 15.4/19.9/21.5, 16.5/16.8/18.6% at 2/4/8 loops (510: 15.1/18.1/19.0, 20.0/23.8/24.9, 15.3/17.0/17.1), rounds 3+ 14.7/19.2/18.2, 14.3/19.1/20.2, 19.5/19.3/20.6. Held-out greedy after RL 0.986/0.977/0.985 (510: 0.984/0.986/0.985). pass@64 at 8 loops by length, seed 0: 108/129/380/99/23/6/1 at lengths 7-13 (510 seed 0: 104/114/389/106/24/5/1). 7 patch lines, one of them code; pods 74-80 min, about $1.90 plus a $0.08 bench. Next: separate the two remaining readings at equal RL rounds. Either cap the untied control at 10-11 rounds, or give the looped trunk 590's round count by retrying at 2 loops only (cheap rounds; 502 says 2 loops cracks 11% of resistant targets against 16% at 8, at 2.5x less cost per sample): if the looped model then approaches 792 the deficit is RL budget; if it stays near 760 it is tying, and the next architecture question is a core with more distinct functions per loop at the same compute (two alternating shared cores, 9.5M), not a wider one.",
